&lt;h2 id="garden">Garden&lt;/h2>
&lt;p>Commercial restaurant garden.&lt;/p>
&lt;h2 id="keywords">Keywords&lt;/h2>
&lt;ul>
&lt;li>
&lt;a href="https://roman-gardens.github.io/test-drafts/search/?q=tables">tables (support furniture)&lt;/a> (&lt;a class="id" target="_blank" href="http://vocab.getty.edu/page/aat/300039548" title="Art and Architecture Thesaurus (Getty)">AAT:300039548&lt;/a>)
&lt;/li>
&lt;/ul>
&lt;h2 id="garden-description">Garden Description&lt;/h2>
&lt;p>This garden restaurant was strategically located across from the Palaestra. This garden occupied most of the southern part of this &lt;em>insula&lt;/em> and had a masonry &lt;a href="http://vocab.getty.edu/page/aat/300004359" target="_blank">triclinium&lt;/a> (l. medius, 4.90 m; l. imus and summus 4.50m), as well as a round table (1.00 m in diameter) and a square table (0.90m x 0.90m).&lt;/p>
&lt;h2 id="dates">Dates&lt;/h2>
&lt;p>1951-1953.&lt;/p>
